# Architecture boundaries

- MCP entrypoints establish immutable principals. Tool arguments never choose
  an actor or policy profile.
- The Tool Gateway enforces authorization, approvals, leases, schemas, path
  confinement, trusted commands, and redacted audit evidence.
- Machine paths and runtime state use XDG locations.
- Mutable project manifests may reference trusted command IDs but never supply
  shell command strings.
- No automatic approval, merge, push, deploy, service management, or dirty
  worktree cleanup.
